  "abstract": {
    "value": "A Ni-mediated decarboxylative silylation of alkynyl cyclic carbonates used as versatile propargylic surrogates is reported a<sup>f</sup>ording a wide range of highly substituted 2,3- and 3,4-allenol products in good yields. The formal cross-coupling between a tentative intermediate Ni(allenyl) and the silyl reagent was further extended to enantiospeci<sup>fi</sup>c conversions providing access to chiral allene synthons. This protocol marks the <sup>fi</sup>rst Nicatalyzed propargylic silylation proceeding through an $S _ { \\mathrm { N } } 2 ^ { \\prime }$ manifold.",
